        {
          "id": 2528776393,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "That's what I'm trying to work towards and trying to work through block vs record/wiretap vs pcapng and \"Wireshark core\". To me sysdig and systemd_journal (and darwin pending MR) shouldn't be part of \"Wireshark core\" and should be handled with lookup tables.\n\nI'm okay with switch statements for \"Wireshark core\" (REC_TYPE_PACKET, REC_TYPE_FT_SPECIFIC\\_\\[EVENT|REPORT\\], BLOCK_TYPE_SHB, BLOCK_TYPE_IDB, etc), with the default in the switch to be \"lookup table for non-core\", but I could be convinced everything should be a lookup table.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
