        {
          "id": 2529122760,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Currently in pcapng_dump(), REC_TYPE_FT_SPECIFIC\\_\\[EVENT|REPORT\\] are looking up \"block\" handlers in the block_handlers hash table.  All other places that look up in block_handlers are BLOCK_TYPE_XXX, so is that a mistake? (it at least confused me on records vs blocks)  I would argue that the only \"Wireshark core\" record type would be REC_TYPE_PACKET and that all other types would need a registered interface with read/process/write functions.\n\nAnd if REC_TYPE_FT_SPECIFIC\\_\\[EVENT|REPORT\\] are \"generic event types, but currently only support sysdig events\", should there be another layer to make that clearer?\n\nI thought both REC_TYPE_SYSTEMD_JOURNAL_EXPORT and BLOCK_TYPE_SYSTEMD_JOURNAL_EXPORT handling should be moved to systemd_journal.\\[c|h\\], with additional tables created as necessary (a different MR)\n\nI think \"Wireshark core\" (pcapng) block types are the very first few types mentioned in the IETF draft of the pcapng format (\\< 0x07 + 0x0A block)  All others should be in a table that is \"plugin capable, but provided as built in\".\n\nThis MR is trying to move all sysdig functionality into those buckets, but still have REC_TYPE_SYSCALL that has a single \"write\" function (pcapng_write_sysdig_event_block), but reading is handled through \"block types\" (which are handled indirectly through register_pcapng_block_type_handler().",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
